# lf106, the plain-step weaver (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf106
revision 1
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_mb_vale_miremore
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the plain-step weaver
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=plain
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk hums_old_marching_songs
likes plum_tart old_tales fresh_straw misty_dawns
dislikes smoke crowds
fears fire_in_the_linen_shed a_tale_used_to_hide_the_truth
hopes a_clean_shed_with_clear_air a_plum_tart_after_the_shift
topics work +0.5 home +0.3 pastimes +0.3 food +0.2
styles comfort=direct gossip=reluctant refuse=firm tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# pulls flawed #linen# from the #loom#, hums a #march# in time with the #shuttle#, and says plainly when a #tale# leaves out the truth.

words
oath! = Warp and straight step | By the clean shuttle
saying! = Say the flaw before the buyer finds it | A straight step beats a sweet excuse
loom = loom | linen loom
shuttle = shuttle | wooden shuttle
warp = warp | taut warp
weft = weft | crossing weft
thread = thread | linen thread
threads = threads | linen threads
linen = linen | woven linen
cloth = cloth | finished cloth
bolt = bolt | linen bolt
bolts = bolts | linen bolts
hem = hem | narrow hem
edge = edge | rough edge
flaw = flaw | visible flaw
flaws = flaws | visible flaws
knot = knot | tight knot
beam = beam | loom beam
shed = shed | linen shed
work = work | loom work
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | working hands
shift = shift | long shift
march = march | old march
song = song | marching song
songs = songs | old songs
beat = beat | steady beat
step = step | measured step
steps = steps | measured steps
tale = tale | old tale
tales = tales | old tales
truth = truth | plain truth
ending = ending | tidy ending
listener = listener | patient listener
market = market | busy market
stall = stall | market stall
buyer = buyer | careful buyer
seller = seller | market seller
price = price | asking price
coin = coin | saved coin
city = city | Ridgemere
road = road | High Road
gate = gate | town gate
wagon = wagon | supply wagon
crowd = crowd | market crowd
house = house | shared house
home = home | cottage
door = door | cottage door
window = window | open window
floor = floor | clean floor
straw = straw | fresh straw
broom = broom | stiff broom
fire = fire | banked fire
flame = flame | small flame
smoke = smoke | sharp smoke
ash = ash | cold ash
roof = roof | shed roof
table = table | supper table
plate = plate | supper plate
bread = bread | fresh bread
plum = plum | ripe plum
plums = plums | ripe plums
tart = tart | plum tart
slice = slice | warm slice
oven = oven | kitchen oven
cup = cup | small cup
friend = friend | trusted friend
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
visitor = visitor | new visitor
stranger = stranger | unknown face
river = river | Long River
bank = bank | riverbank
eel = eel | river eel
trap = trap | eel trap
water = water | river water
mist = mist | morning mist
dawn = dawn | misty dawn
morning = morning | early morning
evening = evening | quiet evening
rain = rain | light rain
wind = wind | field wind
field = field | open field
day = day | long day
hour = hour | short hour
bench = bench | wooden bench
wagons = wagons | passing wagons
loaf = loaf | fresh loaf
night = night | dark night
sun = sun | rising sun
father = father | older father
merchant = merchant | passing merchant
festival = festival | town festival
jar = jar | ale jar

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : The #city# puts #smoke# in the air and calls it industry. | I need room to breathe while I #work#.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : A #crowd# spilling drink does not improve a #song#. | I leave before the shouting begins.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : I have seen an empty #bench# kept from a tired #hand#. | A full #table# should have room for one more.
opinion @1 merchants against 3 : A #seller# raises the #price# of #bread# while my #wages# stay short. | I will tell them exactly what I think.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : A new #hand# can learn the #loom#, but no one should lose a #shift# without warning. | Speak the arrangement plainly.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : The #road# brings #bolts# to buyers. | It also brings #smoke# from passing #wagons#.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : I will answer a #stranger# honestly. | They can decide whether they like it.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Each season asks more #coin# for the same #loaf#. | I have kept the old #price# marks.
line @1 greet : #greet#. That #bolt# has a visible #flaw#. | #greet#. Keep the #door# open; the #smoke# is back.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : Come in. The #tart# has cooled enough. | I know your #steps# on this #floor#.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : The #mist# was thick at the #gate#. | #greet#. My #shuttle# is already moving.
line @1 greet.return : You returned before I cut the rough #edge#. | The #fire# is banked now.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There is a #slice# by the #table#. | Step inside; the #straw# is clean.
line @1 again.open : I have not changed my view of that #cloth#. | Is the #market# still crowded?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I need to mark this #flaw#. | Shut the #gate# behind you.
line @1 farewell.return : Come for the last #slice# later. | The #shed# air should be clearer tomorrow.
line @1 react.news : Tell me what you know, plainly. | Start with what happened at the #gate#.
line @1 react.news.new : No one in this #house# brought me that word. | Was a #wagon# involved?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard the first part at the #market#. | This makes the sequence clearer.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That #tale# has an easy #ending# and a missing middle. | Who can account for the gap?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry. I will not dress this up with a #song#. | Sit here while I put the #work# down.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That is good news, without any need to embellish it. | I will cut the #tart#.
line @1 answer.how : The #loom# is sound and the #floor# is clean. | I found a little #mist# on the #road#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : This #weft# needs my full attention. | I am cutting the bad #thread# out.
line @1 ask.how : Did the #road# treat you honestly? | Has your #house# had a quiet #morning#?
line @1 sympathise : I can sit here without asking for details. | A warm #cup# may help.
line @1 reassure : The #cloth# can be rewoven from the last good #knot#. | The #smoke# will clear with the #window# open.
line @1 decline : No. I will not call flawed #linen# sound. | I need the #price# written before agreeing.
line @1 accept_decline : Understood. I will leave the #bolt# on the #beam#. | Then we can settle it after #evening#.
line @1 thank : You carried the #straw# before the #rain# reached it. | I appreciate a plain answer.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It was one #slice#, and I had plenty. | The #broom# was in my #hand#.
line @1 preclose : I need to sweep the #floor# before supper. | The last #shuttle# pass is waiting.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #tale# has more knots than this #warp#. | That marching #step# would trip over a #straw#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. That #edge# is rough. | #bc_fair_enough#. We can check the #bolt# again.
line @1 give.advice : Mark a #flaw# while the #cloth# is still on the #beam#. | Put fresh #straw# over a dry #floor#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Do not walk the #road# alone at #night#. | Keep near the #wagons# at the #gate#.
scene plain_flaw
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I tell a #buyer# about a #flaw# before they find it. | A short sale is better than a long quarrel.
b : Do they still buy? | Does anyone object?
a : Often, at the right #price#. | Only those who wanted it hidden.

scene rough_edge
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #edge# of a #bolt# can look smooth while the #threads# pull loose. | I run my fingers along it before cutting.
b : Can you mend it? | Does it take long?
a : With a new #hem#. | Less than an argument later.

scene marching_shuttle
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I hum an old #march# when the #shuttle# runs evenly. | The #beat# changes when a #knot# catches.
b : Does that help? | Who taught the song?
a : I hear the mistake sooner. | I learned it at #home#.

scene smoke_in_shed
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Smoke from the #fire# can settle in the #linen#. | I open the #door# and stop the #loom# until the air clears.
b : Does cloth keep the smell? | Has a fire started?
a : Longer than it should. | Not while I am watching.

scene clean_straw
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fresh #straw# on a dry #floor# keeps mud out of our #house#. | I change it when the #rain# has passed.
b : Does it stay neat? | Who helps?
a : For a #day# or two. | Anyone who tracked mud in.

scene plum_tart
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #plum# #tart# should hold its fruit in thick pieces. | I do not want a sweet crust hiding an empty middle.
b : Do you make it? | Do you share?
a : When the #oven# is free. | After I keep one #slice#.

scene old_tale_truth
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I enjoy an old #tale# until the teller claims it happened yesterday. | Then I ask which part is true.
b : Does that spoil the story? | Do they answer?
a : A good teller can laugh. | The honest ones do.

scene forgotten_ending
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #stranger# once told us a #tale# with an ending too neat for the facts. | I asked what became of the missing #wagon#.
b : Was there a wagon? | Did the stranger mind?
a : That was the point. | Enough to tell the rest.

scene mist_gate
when topic=weather here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Mist hides the #gate# at #dawn# but not the sound of a #wagon#. | I follow the wheel ruts in.
b : Have you lost your way? | Is it cold?
a : Not on this #road#. | Until the #sun# rises.

scene clear_air
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : After #rain#, the #wind# clears #smoke# from the #shed#. | I leave the #window# open until the #linen# smells clean.
b : Does rain slow the work? | Do you like it?
a : Only if the #roof# leaks. | When the air improves.

scene river_trap
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I know a bend in the #river# where an #eel# #trap# sits properly. | I set it below the shallow #bank#.
b : Do you catch many? | Is it your secret?
a : Enough to justify the walk. | I have told you now.

scene shared_cottage
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our shared #house# has #loom# hands and paper hands at one #table#. | I say when the #floor# needs sweeping.
b : Does anyone mind? | Do they help?
a : They can mind and still hear me. | Usually by #evening#.

scene father_lesson
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #father# taught me to speak before a small problem grows. | I remember that when a #thread# frays.
b : Did he weave? | Was he strict?
a : He knew how to mend. | Plainer than strict.

scene market_crowd
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #crowd# at the #market# makes every #seller# louder than the next. | I buy what I need and leave.
b : Do you miss the stories? | What if it is busy?
a : I can hear them later. | I wait by the #gate#.

scene road_price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #merchant# blamed the #road# for a higher #price#. | The same #wagon# had brought the last #bolt# more cheaply.
b : Did you say so? | What did they answer?
a : To their face. | That costs had changed.

scene festival_spill
when topic=pastimes here.day=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At the #festival# a spilled #jar# ran across the #floor# near the #song#. | I left before someone slipped.
b : Was anyone hurt? | Did you clean it?
a : Not while I watched. | I warned the keeper.

scene shed_fire
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Once a #flame# rose too high beside stacked #linen#. | I moved the #bolts# before anyone had time to argue.
b : Did the shed burn? | Were you afraid?
a : The walls held. | Enough to move quickly.

story marked_flaw [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : I found a thin #thread# running across a finished #bolt#.
  : I marked the #flaw# before a #buyer# arrived and offered the #cloth# at a lower #price#.
  ask : Did they take it?
  b : Fair dealing.
  : They did, after seeing the mark.

story smoky_morning [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : Smoke filled the #shed# while the #loom# was set.
  : I opened the #door#, moved the #linen# away, and waited for clean air.
  ask : Did you lose the day?
  b : Better to stop.
  : An #hour#, and no #cloth# spoiled.

story river_bend [topic=pastimes self.age>=18]
  : I moved an #eel# #trap# from a shallow #bank# to a deeper bend.
  : The first place had left it nearly dry by #morning#.
  ask : Did you catch one?
  b : You found the better water.
  : Enough for a meal after the #shift#.

rule @bark_flaw
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Mark that #flaw# before it leaves. | The #edge# needs another look.

rule @bark_smoke
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Open the #door#; I smell #smoke#. | Keep the #bolts# clear of the #fire#.

rule @bark_straw
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say This #straw# has gone damp. | The #floor# wants a #broom#.

rule @bark_tart
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say Save the last #slice#. | A #plum# #tart# ought to show its fruit.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I am checking this #bolt# for #flaws#. | #greet#. Leave the #door# open if you smell #smoke#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Back again? The #edge# was rough after all. | I remember you; the #shed# air is clearer now.
dlg @1 resident.job : I weave #linen# at the #shed# and mark flaws before it sells. | My #shuttle# keeps time with an old #march#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I will finish this #hem#. | #saying.capitalize#. Watch the #gate# on your way.
graft resident.hub
choice Why mark a flaw? -> flaw
node flaw
say A #buyer# should know what is in a #bolt#. I mark the #flaw# before anyone pays for the #cloth#.
free
choice What is that tune? -> march
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node march
say An old #march# I learned at #home#. Its #beat# lets me hear when the #shuttle# catches.
choice Back to the loom. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #warp# is set. | #greet#. I have marked the rough #edge#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. The #floor# needs sweeping. | The #tart# will be ready after the #shift#.
